\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Coordinate multiplicities for a reducible charge}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In \ref{fdip-008B}, choose an ordered basis of each
multiplicity space #{M_\lambda} and set
#{n_\lambda=\dim M_\lambda}. Transport along that basis is a
linear identification #{M_\lambda\cong\mathbb C^{n_\lambda}}.
It carries the vector-space isomorphism to
##{\mathcal M_R\cong
 \bigoplus_\lambda
 \operatorname{Hom}(\mathbb C^{n_\lambda},\mathcal M_{R_\lambda}).}
The basis choice is not part of the isomorphism stated there,
and this coordinate form is not claimed to be unitary.}
